  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nA lathe Facing that only faces the end of a bar was refused at the post when the bar had a groove anywhere along it (#1408). The finish-envelope verdict (law f) reported the groove as the Facing's rest. The cause is in the scan's hidden-rest half, which measures every Z-occluded top against the nearest nose centre:\n\n1. **The scan never turned the work.** The groove floor's rim across the spindle, at (-r, 0, z_floor), was read against a path written in the y = 0, x >= 0 meridian. The issue's figures (17.05 / 10.28 / 15.56) are exactly that distance.\n2. **Once turned, the near side was still 14 mm below the faced band.** No nose of the Facing travels that far down the spindle.\n\nThe Profile half (austin62jake's comment) shares cause 1: 12.49 / 12.76 on the shaft. Once the work turns, two smaller readings remain. Neither is rest the op owes:\n\n- the groove floor's inner corner, which a 0.8 nose cannot reach (0.33 mm, `r(sqrt2 - 1)`);\n- the Profile Rough's own 0.25 leave on the groove floor (0.287 on the shaft; 1.06 on the 2 mm near-top groove, which the rough plus its leave cannot enter).\n\nThe visible (ridge) half already lets both stand. They reached the hidden half only through Z-occlusion, and Z-occlusion means nothing to a tool that comes in radially.\n\n## The fix\n\n- `VerifyContext::lathe_axis` (new, default `None`): the spindle a turning nose op's kernel fitted. `operation::turning_axis::lathe_axis_of` sets it for every `Family::Turn` op whose tool states a nose radius, by the same `turning::Frame::about` reading the lathe sim uses. A source no axis fits gets `None`.\n- `stock_sim::envelope_scan_turned(facets, moves, r, tol, (axis, leave))` (`envelope_scan_centers` is now `(None, 0.0)` of it). Law (f) passes `cx.lathe_axis` and `cx.stock_to_leave` for nose-centre paths.\n- `stock_sim::scan_turned` (new, 174 lines) changes only the hidden-rest half, with four clauses:\n  1. **The work turns.** Each hidden top is read at itself and at its two turns into the path's meridian plane. Every sample lies on the top's orbit, so the reading can only be at or above the true orbit distance. It may over-read (a refusal) but never hides rest, even on a path that leaves its plane.\n  2. **The band.** A top farther along the spindle than every nose centre, by more than the nose plus the scan floor plus the arcs' bulge, is excused.\n  3. **The crease.** A top the nose cannot touch is excused. This uses the ridge law's own accessibility test (`ridge::Access::reachable`, the tangent ball along the normal).\n  4. **The leave.** A rough's `stock_to_leave` is its promise, and the crease test reads the ball grown by the leave.\n- Gouge half, visible half and every mill path are unchanged. Without a spindle the scan is bit for bit the old one; this is pinned.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1408-turned-envelope-hidden-floor.md`. It covers why this is not a switch to `Mode::Revolve` (that is the blade's boxcar law, and the registry already keeps the nose kinds on law f), why the axis is not world Z, and why the hidden half is kept.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/turning_hidden_floor.rs` builds the issue's 64-segment bars on a lathe document with d20 x 50 stock and TN-1600-0R8, and runs them through `posting::post_script` with `fanuc-lathe.cps`:\n\n- `a_facing_over_a_grooved_bar_posts`: groove, groove near the top, shaft. Facing posts.\n- `the_shafts_facing_and_profiles_post`: shaft. Facing, Profile Rough and Profile Finish are clean, and the program is written.\n- `the_profiles_post_over_both_grooves`: groove and groove near the top, with Facing, Rough and Finish.\n- `bars_without_a_groove_post_as_before`: plain and stepped post (stepped with Rough and Finish). The bar wider at the free end has no findings.\n- `a_facing_that_gouges_the_grooved_bar_still_blocks_by_name`: Facing plane at 47. The `Envelope` warning carries a gouge over 0.5 mm, and the post is refused with \"post blocked ... F2 ... finish envelope\".\n\n`crates/sim/tests/turned_hidden_rest.rs`:\n\n- `a_groove_floor_under_the_facing_band_is_not_its_rest`: the unturned scan reads more than 15 mm; the turned scan reads at or under the gate; the gouge half is bit-identical.\n- `a_hidden_floor_the_nose_could_reach_inside_its_band_still_convicts`: a nose that rides the OD past the 3 mm groove inside its own band reads more than 3 mm of rest, with leave 0 and with leave 0.25.\n- `without_a_spindle_the_scan_is_the_old_one_bit_for_bit`\n- `law_f_still_blocks_a_real_rest_and_a_real_gouge_by_name`: through `verify` with `lathe_axis` set, both a real rest and a real gouge give a blocking `finish envelope` warning.\n\nAlso `scan_turned` unit tests: the band/orbit geometry, and a path on the axis or non-finite.\n\n## Mutation check (standing rule: each new excuse and guard deleted gives RED, restored gives GREEN)\n\n| Mutation | Red tests |\n|---|---|\n| M1 delete the band excuse | sim `a_groove_floor_under_the_facing_band_is_not_its_rest`, `law_f_still_blocks_...`; app `a_facing_over_a_grooved_bar_posts`, `the_profiles_post_over_both_grooves`, `the_shafts_facing_and_profiles_post` |\n| M2 delete the orbit (turned) reading | app `the_profiles_post_over_both_grooves`, `the_shafts_facing_and_profiles_post` |\n| M3 delete the nose-accessibility (crease) excuse | app `the_profiles_post_over_both_grooves`, `the_shafts_facing_and_profiles_post` |\n| M4 leave not forgiven (`leave = 0.0`) | app `the_profiles_post_over_both_grooves`, `the_shafts_facing_and_profiles_post` |\n| M5 crease test on the bare nose, not nose + leave | app `the_profiles_post_over_both_grooves` |\n| M6 app passes no spindle (`lathe_axis: None`, i.e. the pre-fix verdict) | app `a_facing_over_a_grooved_bar_posts`, `the_profiles_post_over_both_grooves`, `the_shafts_facing_and_profiles_post` |\n| restored | all 4 sim + 5 app tests GREEN |\n\nThe two \"still blocks\" tests are guards against over-excusing: they stay green under every deletion above, by design.\n\n## Goldens\n\nNo golden changed. Paths are untouched (only the verdict reads differently), and every app `turning*` and `lathe*` suite passed with a clean tree after it (39 suites, `lathe_post` goldens included).\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app` on every `turning*` / `lathe*` suite: 39 suites, all ok.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim --test turned_hidden_rest` and `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test turning_hidden_floor`: ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green, 25.5 min wall (sim 184 s, motion 6 s, app 1209 s, ui 130 s; 0 failed)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Boring, Chamfer, Taper and Multi-Pass also get the spindle (same `Family::Turn` + nose door). Their suites pass, but no new fixture puts a groove under them.\n- A groove the nose fits but the insert's trailing geometry cannot enter is still judged as reachable. This errs toward refusing.\n- The MCP repro was not re-run through `camcraft-cli`. The app tests drive the same commands and the same post gate.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 54); this branch is cut from upstream/main 3f6ecb4a.\n\nChangelog: A lathe Facing (and the Profile kinds) on a grooved bar is no longer refused at the post: the envelope verdict reads hidden floors as the turning work sees them, out-of-band, nose-unreachable and leave-covered tops excused; a real gouge or owed rest in the op's own band still blocks (#1408)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1408\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
